<header class="post-hero">
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag tag-purple">Diffusion Language Models</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Continuous Latent Space</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Flow Matching</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Cola DLM: When Diffusion Stops Recovering Tokens and Starts Thinking in Latents</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every prior "continuous" language model still uses diffusion to recover noisy token embeddings — observation recovery in disguise. Cola DLM (ByteDance Seed, 2026) breaks that mold: a Text VAE compresses text into compact latent blocks, then a block-causal DiT learns a continuous prior over those latents through flow matching. The decoder handles token realization. The result: hierarchical semantic decomposition that scales past AR and discrete DLMs at 2000+ EFLOPs.</p>
