<p>Why does this matter? When diffusion targets latent <em>priors</em> rather than token-aligned observations, the model gets three things: a continuous space that naturally captures semantic geometry, no fixed left-to-right inductive bias, and a clean theoretical decomposition into "what to say" (prior) and "how to say it" (decoder).</p>
</section>

<section id="s-arch" data-code="arch">
<div class="section-no">02 — Architecture</div>
<h2>Two Training Stages, One Hierarchical Generative Model</h2>
<p>Cola DLM is not a cascade of three independent modules — it's a single hierarchical probabilistic model trained in two stages. Stage 1 builds a stable latent–text interface; Stage 2 learns a conditional prior on top of it.</p>

